[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-160771"] :question/problem "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\sqrt{2+t}\\,i+\\frac{1}{3+t}\\,j+(1+{t}^{2})\\,k.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\sqrt{2+t}$ is $t\\in [-2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\frac{1}{3+t}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,-3)\\cup (-3,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $1+{t}^{2}$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14076578/assets/01998bcc54d297275af928b2467e7bcc077c84fd595567f5b3ff5bf89d38ec7b.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in [-2,\\infty ).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-162687/selection/9b3f8931a3536ec48d21f391c8a958a6e169d712a9a94dd62a81eaa5dae83c07" :answer/id #uuid "1036eaad-7f83-5f39-a828-244cc85af613" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in [-2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162687/selection/30bbc689c827313dd24ca035c2cdff693bad7e54c82d90e845f687cf2d7d1562" :answer/id #uuid "8509d099-9563-5608-bb8d-6a78d6c2a513" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\infty ,2)\\cup (2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162687/selection/e1d49f07b54c7e56492f52af3b91776dae2cd03f3b7af03d87381acca4b49288" :answer/id #uuid "c42a05f8-fcf2-579a-bf98-57f256bc1afa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\infty ,2]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162687/selection/7cbdcc5613e9aaa4fe8ecda1da307985c8430babf39d99a2747e771d834ce8ac" :answer/id #uuid "e1607671-4540-5f07-b79e-b72be46471cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "t\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (-2,\\infty )" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16268